<figure class="wal-progress" aria-labelledby="physical-wal-title" data-physical-wal>
  <figcaption id="physical-wal-title"><span>Figure 1</span> A durable commit can still read as 20.00</figcaption>
  <div class="scene">
    <div class="primary"><strong>Primary · history H</strong><span>WAL sender → network → A's WAL receiver</span><b>U · P7 → 22.00</b><b>C · commit</b></div>
    <p class="direction">↓ the same WAL passes through separate stages on A</p>
    <div class="lanes">
      {['Received · receiver memory', 'Written · operating system', 'Flushed · durable WAL', 'Replayed · recovery process'].map((name, i) => <div class="lane"><strong>{name}</strong><div class="records"><span class="included">Earlier</span><span data-record={i} data-live>U</span><span data-record={i} data-live>C</span></div><span data-stage={i} data-live>Before U</span></div>)}
    </div>
    <div class="answer"><span>A · new read snapshot</span><b data-price data-live>20.00</b><span data-verdict data-live>C is not here yet</span></div>
  </div>
  <p class="explanation" data-explanation data-live aria-live="polite">P7 starts at 20.00. Follow U, the update, and C, its commit, from the primary to A.</p>
  <div class="controls" role="group" aria-label="Controls for figure 1"><button data-play data-live>Play</button><button data-back>Back</button><button data-next>Next</button><button data-reset>Reset</button><span data-step data-live>1 / 6</span></div>
  <div class="hold" data-hold aria-hidden="true"><span></span></div>
  <p class="caption">A selected schedule, with symbolic records and no time or byte scale. A tick marks a record included at that stage. The final read uses a new snapshot; an earlier report can still see 20.00.</p>
  <details><summary>Figure as text</summary><ol><li>The primary generates U and C.</li><li>A receives both in memory.</li><li>A writes both to its WAL file, possibly only into operating-system cache.</li><li>A flushes both. The commit is recoverable, but not yet visible.</li><li>Recovery replays U; without C replayed, the new price is still uncommitted here.</li><li>Recovery replays C. A new snapshot reads 22.00.</li></ol></details>
</figure>
<script>
  import { stepper } from '../figures/stepper.mjs';
  const root = document.querySelector('[data-physical-wal]');
  if (root instanceof HTMLElement) {
    const explanations = [
      'The primary has generated U and C. A still has only the earlier history and reads 20.00.',
      'The WAL receiver has received U and C in memory. This alone does not establish a durable copy.',
      'A has written U and C to its WAL file. The operating system may still hold those bytes in volatile cache.',
      'The flush reaches C. A can recover the committed price from surviving WAL, but a new read still returns 20.00.',
      'Recovery has applied U, but not its commit C. The 22.00 version is not yet committed for an ordinary reader on A.',
      'Recovery has applied C too. A new snapshot can now read 22.00; an already established earlier snapshot need not change.'
    ];
    stepper(root, { steps: () => 6, draw(step) {
      for (let i=0;i<4;i++) {
        const through = i < 3 ? step >= i+1 : step === 5;
        root.querySelectorAll(`[data-record="${i}"]`).forEach((el,j) => {
          const included = through || (i===3 && step===4 && j===0);
          el.classList.toggle('included',included);
          el.textContent = `${included ? '✓ ' : ''}${j===0?'U':'C'}`;
        });
        root.querySelector(`[data-stage="${i}"]`).textContent = through?'Through C':i===3&&step===4?'Through U':'Before U';
      }
      root.querySelector('[data-price]').textContent = step===5?'22.00':'20.00';
      root.querySelector('[data-verdict]').textContent = step===5?'C is visible':step>=3?'C is durable; replay is behind':'No durable C established';
      root.querySelector('[data-explanation]').textContent=explanations[step];
    }});
  }
</script>
<style>
  figure { margin:2.2rem 0; font: .83rem/1.55 var(--font-sans); }
  figcaption { font:500 1.2rem/1.4 var(--font-serif); margin-bottom:.7rem; }
  figcaption > span { font:.65rem var(--font-mono); text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:.08em; color:var(--color-text-secondary); margin-right:.7rem; }
  .scene { border:1px solid var(--color-rule-strong); padding:1.2rem; background:var(--color-surface-alt); }
  .primary { display:grid; grid-template-columns:1fr auto auto; gap:.5rem; }
  .primary > span { grid-column:1/-1; color:var(--color-text-secondary); order:1; }
  .primary b { font: .8rem/1.5 var(--font-mono); border:1px solid var(--color-rule-strong); padding:.3rem .5rem; }
  .direction { margin:1rem 0; color:var(--color-text-secondary); font:inherit; }
  .lane { display:grid; grid-template-columns:1.8fr 1.3fr .7fr; align-items:center; gap:.7rem; padding:.8rem 0; border-top:1px solid var(--color-rule-strong); }
  .lane strong { font-weight:500; }
  .lane > span { font:.73rem var(--font-mono); text-align:right; }
  .records { display:flex; gap:.25rem; }
  .records span { border:1px dashed var(--color-text-secondary); padding:.25rem .4rem; font:.74rem/1.5 var(--font-mono); flex:1; text-align:center; }
  .records .included { border-style:solid; border-color:var(--color-accent); color:var(--color-accent); }
  .answer { margin-top:1rem; padding-top:1rem; border-top:2px solid var(--color-rule-strong); display:grid; grid-template-columns:1fr auto; gap:.3rem; }
  .answer b { font:500 1.8rem var(--font-serif); grid-column:2; grid-row:1/3; }
  .answer > span:last-child { color:var(--color-text-secondary); }
  .explanation { font:inherit; min-height:4.6em; }
  .controls { display:flex; flex-wrap:wrap; gap:.45rem; align-items:center; }
  button { border:1px solid var(--color-rule-strong); background:var(--color-surface-alt); color:var(--color-text); font:inherit; padding:.4rem .65rem; cursor:pointer; }
  button[aria-disabled="true"] { opacity:.5; }
  button:focus-visible,summary:focus-visible { outline:2px solid var(--color-accent); outline-offset:3px; }
  [data-step] { margin-left:auto; font:.75rem var(--font-mono); }
  .hold { height:2px; background:var(--color-rule); margin:.6rem 0; }
  .hold span { display:block; width:0; height:100%; background:var(--color-accent); }
  .caption { font:.8rem/1.6 var(--font-sans); color:var(--color-text-secondary); }
  summary { cursor:pointer; }
  @media(max-width:550px) { .scene{padding:.8rem}.primary{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr}.primary strong{grid-column:1/-1}.lane{grid-template-columns:1fr auto}.records{grid-row:2;grid-column:1/-1}.lane > span{font-size:.7rem}.explanation{min-height:7em} }
</style>
